  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "What is the range of the function $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{30}^{\u2218})+4?$",
  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{30}^{\u2218})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and then adding $4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{30}^{\u2218})\\le 1 \\\\ 2 & \\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{30}^{\u2218})\\ge -2 \\\\ 6 & \\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+{30}^{\u2218})+4\\ge 2 \\\\ 2 & \\le y\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [2,6].$",
